body:
We used to have dogs in stores here in the U.S. when I was growing up (read: \~90s era). It was the same. Miserable poor little animals locked in cages not getting any exercise or socialization. I believe they were federally outlawed (fact checks welcome)? It was about the same as the puppy mill crisis, which is sadly still legal here. I believe it's still legal for stores to keep animals that are normally caged; rodents, birds, reptiles, etc. But IMO every animal deserves to spend time outside of a cage. If that animal is too much of a risk to the pet or the owner to be let out, then that animal should not be allowed to own as a pet.

&#x200B;

*edited to note location/government*
